Feature: Forecast ERP SQL logic for f_inv_movmnt report generation

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog is purgo_databricks and schema is purgo_playground
    And the mapping table inv_txn_mapping.xlsx defines field logic for f_order and f_inv_movmnt
    And supporting tables/views include vw_calculated_allocated_qty, f_inv_movmnt_apl_qty, f_inv_movmnt_apl_qty_result, f_inv_movmnt_apl_qty_test

  Scenario Outline: Generate forecast report row for f_inv_movmnt with mapped fields
    Given a left outer join between f_inv_movmnt and f_order on <ord_id>, <ord_line_nbr>, <b_dt>
    And allocated_qty is calculated as sum(qty_1, qty_2, qty_3, qty_4) for each order and line number
    And delivery_dt is set to current date in yyyymmdd format
    And sched_dt is sourced from yeblen.drdat in yyyymmdd format
    And flag_key is true if txn_id is present, else false
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the output row contains:
      | txn_id | allocated_qty | delivery_dt | sched_dt | flag_key |
    And allocated_qty is a decimal, default 0.00 if missing
    And delivery_dt and sched_dt are decimals (38,0) in yyyymmdd format
    And flag_key is boolean (true/false)
    And all data quality rules are enforced per mapping

    Examples:
      | ord_id   | ord_line_nbr | b_dt      | qty_1 | qty_2 | qty_3 | qty_4 | txn_id      | yeblen_drdat | expected_allocated_qty | expected_flag_key |
      | ORD001   | 10           | 20240601  | 5.0   | 2.0   | 0.0   | 1.0   | TXN123      | 20240605     | 8.0                   | true             |
      | ORD002   | 20           | 20240602  | 0.0   | 0.0   | 0.0   | 0.0   |             | 20240606     | 0.0                   | false            |
      | ORD003   | 30           | 20240603  | 3.5   | 2.5   | 1.0   | 0.0   | TXN456      | 20240607     | 7.0                   | true             |
      | ORD004   | 40           | 20240604  | null  | 1.0   | 2.0   | 3.0   | TXN789      | 20240608     | 6.0                   | true             |
      | ORD005   | 50           | 20240605  | 2.0   | null  | null  | null  |             | 20240609     | 2.0                   | false            |

  Scenario: Validate allocated_qty decimal type and default value
    Given allocated_qty is calculated from qty_1, qty_2, qty_3, qty_4
    When any qty_x is missing or null
    Then treat missing values as 0.0
    And allocated_qty is a decimal value
    And if all qty_x are missing, allocated_qty is 0.00

  Scenario: Validate delivery_dt and sched_dt format
    Given delivery_dt and sched_dt are required in yyyymmdd format
    When source date is not in yyyymmdd format
    Then transform to yyyymmdd as decimal(38,0)
    And raise error "Invalid date format for delivery_dt/sched_dt" if transformation fails

  Scenario: Validate flag_key logic
    Given flag_key is true if txn_id is present, else false
    When txn_id is not present or is null
    Then flag_key is false
    When txn_id is present and not null
    Then flag_key is true

  Scenario Outline: Data quality validation for forecast report row
    Given a forecast report row with <allocated_qty>, <delivery_dt>, <sched_dt>, <flag_key>
    When the row is validated
    Then allocated_qty must be decimal, default 0.00
    And delivery_dt and sched_dt must be decimal(38,0) in yyyymmdd format
    And flag_key must be boolean (true/false)
    And if any field fails validation, error message is returned

    Examples:
      | allocated_qty | delivery_dt | sched_dt  | flag_key | expected_error                        |
      | 8.0           | 20240601    | 20240605  | true     |                                       |
      | null          | 20240602    | 20240606  | false    |                                       |
      | 7.0           | 20240603    | 20240607  | true     |                                       |
      | 6.0           | 20240604    | 20240608  | true     |                                       |
      | 2.0           | 20240605    | 20240609  | false    |                                       |
      | "abc"         | 20240610    | 20240611  | true     | "allocated_qty must be decimal"       |
      | 5.0           | "2024-06-12"| 20240613  | true     | "delivery_dt must be yyyymmdd format" |
      | 4.0           | 20240614    | "2024-06-15"| false   | "sched_dt must be yyyymmdd format"    |
      | 3.0           | 20240616    | 20240617  | "yes"    | "flag_key must be boolean"            |

  Scenario: Duplicate order and line number handling
    Given multiple rows with same ord_id and ord_line_nbr
    When generating allocated_qty
    Then sum qty_1, qty_2, qty_3, qty_4 for all matching rows
    And output a single row per unique ord_id and ord_line_nbr

  Scenario: Missing f_order join data
    Given f_inv_movmnt row with no matching f_order entry
    When joining for allocated_qty
    Then allocated_qty is set to 0.00
    And flag_key is false

  Scenario: SQL logic error handling
    Given a SQL execution error occurs (e.g., type mismatch, missing field)
    When generating the forecast report
    Then output error message with field and reason

    Examples:
      | error_type         | field           | reason                        | expected_error_message                  |
      | TypeMismatch       | allocated_qty   | Non-decimal value             | "allocated_qty must be decimal"         |
      | MissingField       | delivery_dt     | Field not found               | "delivery_dt is required"               |
      | FormatError        | sched_dt        | Not yyyymmdd                  | "sched_dt must be yyyymmdd format"      |
      | NullValue          | flag_key        | Null not allowed              | "flag_key must be boolean"              |

  Scenario: Data quality enforcement for valid values
    Given the mapping specifies valid values for each field
    When a field value is outside allowed range or type
    Then error message is returned and row is excluded from report

  Scenario Outline: Representative error path cases for forecast report
    Given input data with <allocated_qty>, <delivery_dt>, <sched_dt>, <flag_key>
    When SQL logic is executed
    Then if any field fails validation, error message is returned

    Examples:
      | allocated_qty | delivery_dt | sched_dt  | flag_key | expected_error_message                  |
      | "abc"         | 20240601    | 20240605  | true     | "allocated_qty must be decimal"         |
      | 8.0           | "2024-06-01"| 20240605  | true     | "delivery_dt must be yyyymmdd format"   |
      | 7.0           | 20240603    | "2024-06-07"| true    | "sched_dt must be yyyymmdd format"      |
      | 6.0           | 20240604    | 20240608  | "yes"    | "flag_key must be boolean"              |
      | null          | 20240605    | 20240609  | false    |                                         |

  Scenario: Output structure for forecast report
    Given the forecast report is generated for f_inv_movmnt
    Then output contains columns:
      | txn_id | allocated_qty | delivery_dt | sched_dt | flag_key |
    And all columns conform to mapping and data quality rules

# END
